---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Systems Gallery"
tagline: Twelve real interactions between Earth's spheres, each one a diagram waiting to be drawn
extraStylesheets:
  - /assets/block-page.css
breadcrumbs:
  - { url: /, label: Home }
  - { url: /units/, label: Units }
  - { url: /units/unit-1/, label: "Unit 1: Earth and Universe" }
  - { label: "Systems Gallery" }
returnTo:
  - { url: /units/unit-1/block-2b/, label: "Unit 1 · Block 2b" }
  - { url: /units/unit-1/block-7/, label: "Unit 1 · Block 7" }
---

<div class="prose">

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">How to use a card</div>
  <ol>
    <li>Pick one card. Six are in Chennai, six are global; the first arrow is already written so you do not start blank.</li>
    <li>Copy its note frame onto paper: four lines, in that order.</li>
    <li>Draw it the same way you drew Step 4 to Step 7 in <a href="/units/unit-1/reading-build-a-systems-diagram/">Build Your First Systems Diagram</a>: two circles and the first arrow, the return arrow, the sign, then the next sphere.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

</div>

<div class="entry-grid gallery-grid">
  {%- for c in systemsGallery.cards %}
  <article class="entry-card gallery-card" id="{{ c.id }}">
    <div class="entry-title">{{ c.title }}</div>
    <div class="entry-meta">{{ c.where }} · {{ c.spheres | join(" and ") }}</div>
    <dl class="gc-fields">
      <dt>First arrow</dt>
      <dd>{{ c.firstArrow }}</dd>
      <dt>Return arrow</dt>
      <dd>{{ c.returnArrowHint }}</dd>
      <dt>Sign</dt>
      <dd>{{ c.signHint }}</dd>
      <dt>Grow to</dt>
      <dd>{{ c.growTo }}</dd>
      <dt>Sources</dt>
      <dd>
        <ul class="gc-sources">
          {%- for s in c.sources %}
          <li><a href="{{ s.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ s.label }}</a><span class="gc-origin">Origin: {{ s.origin }}</span></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </dd>
      <dt>Note frame</dt>
      <dd>
        <ol class="gc-frame">
          {%- for line in c.noteFrame %}
          <li>{{ line }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </article>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="prose">

<div class="callout good">
  <div class="callout-title">Where this goes</div>
  <p><a href="/units/unit-1/block-7/">Block 7</a> is where the systems-thinking strand gets graded: the last field of every habitability criterion asks where it can fail, and that is a feedback loop in disguise. A gallery diagram with a signed loop and a cited source is exactly the evidence it wants. Keep the drawing, keep the source's Origin line, and bring both.</p>
</div>

</div>
